    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense for May 21st hinges on the elite production expected from **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries an 82.08 efficiency score into his matchup against Carlos Rod\u00f3n. Despite the lefty-lefty dynamic, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2019s impressive .376 xwOBA makes him our clear anchor; the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and the high-leverage #2 spot in the lineup projects him for significant run-scoring potential. Supporting him are **Nolan Schanuel** (64.29) and **Josh Lowe** (64.94), both of whom benefit from a matchup against Luis Severino. **Josh Lowe** is particularly intriguing; while his #9 position in the lineup historically drags his score, his elite speed profile and the dynamic platoon advantage against Severino provide a high ceiling for stolen bases\u2014our most critical scarcity category.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the bottom half of the lineup, where **Dominic Smith** (53.57) and **Nasim Nunez** (52.46) represent marginal starts. **Dominic Smith** narrowly edged out internal bench options by leveraging a strong platoon advantage against Sandy Alcantara. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** remains in the lineup primarily for his speed-first utility; while his efficiency is limited by a #8 order position and a tough matchup against David Peterson, his ability to manufacture stolen bases is essential to our 5x5 Roto strategy. Conversely, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (51.75) struggled in our projections due to a negative platoon split against Peterson, yet he remains active to ensure we maintain sufficient positional coverage while awaiting the return of core contributors like **Luis Robert Jr.** from the IL.\n\nManagers must remain vigilant as all current projections are based on \"Lineup Pending\" status; official lineup confirmation is critical, as any demotion to the bottom of the order for **Liam Hicks** (47.37) or **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** would trigger a move to the bench to preserve our game caps. While we are currently deprived of heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Andy Pages** due to team off-days, the squad is positioned to prioritize efficiency in SB and R today. We are closely monitoring the weather and confirmed lineups for any late-breaking changes that would necessitate pulling **Liam Hicks** in favor of available depth like **Drake Baldwin** or **Jacob Wilson**.",
